item/28x885gw [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 16. Stark N, Hayirli T, Bhanja A, Kerrissey M, Hardy J, Peabody CR. Unprecedented training: experience of residents during the COVID-19 pandemic. Ann Emerg Med. 2022;79(5):488–94. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Cook DA, Brydges R, Zendejas B, Hamstra SJ, Hatala R. Mastery learning for Health professionals using technology-enhanced Simulation: a systematic review and Meta-analysis. Acad Med. 2013;88(8):1178–86. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Kardong-Edgren S, Swoboda S, Sullivan N. Simulation as Clinical Replacement: Contemporary Approaches in Healthcare Professional Education. In: Nestel D, Reedy G, McKenna L, Gough S, editors. Clinical Education for the Health Professions [Internet]. Singapore: Springer Singapore; 2020 [cited 2024 Mar 7]. pp. 1–17. http://link.springer.com/ 10.1007/978-981-13-6106-7_44-1 19. Nadir N, Kim J, Cassara M, Hrdy M, Zaveri P, Wong AH, et al. Simulation-based emergency medicine education in the era of physical distancing. AEM Educ Train. 2021;5(3):e10586. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Albott CS, Wozniak JR, McGlinch BP, Wall MH, Gold BS, Vinogradov S. Battle buddies: Rapid Deployment of a Psychological Resilience Intervention for Health Care workers during the COVID-19 pandemic. Anesth Analg. 2020;131(1):43–54. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Monette D, Macias-Konstantopoulos W, Brown D, Raja A, Takayesu J. A Video-based Debriefing Program to Support Emergency Medicine Clinician Well-being During the COVID-19 Pandemic. West J Emerg Med [Internet]. 2020 Sep 25 [cited 2024 Mar 7];21(6). https://escholarship.org/uc/item/9b65n8kr [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials Supplementary Material 1 (25.7KB, docx) Data Availabili