Google Scholar ] 28. Friedman M. The Use of Ranks to Avoid the Assumption of Normality Implicit in the Analysis of Variance. J. Am. Stat. Assoc. [Internet]. 1937;32:675. Available from: http://www.jstor.org/stable/2279372?origin=crossref 29. Wilcoxon F. Individual Comparisons by Ranking Methods Author ( s ): Frank Wilcoxon Published by : International Biometric Society. Biometrics Bull. [Internet]. 1945;1:80–3. Available from: http://www.jstor.org/stable/3001968 30. Bisgaard CH, Rubak SLM, Rodt SA, Petersen JAK, Musaeus P. The effects of graduate competency-based education and mastery learning on patient care and return on investment: a narrative review of basic anesthetic procedures. BMC Med Educ. 2018;18(1):154. doi: 10.1186/s12909-018-1262-7. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Data Availability Statement The datasets used and/or analyzed during the current study are available from the corresponding author on reasonable request.',66,'2025-10-15 11:23:06','2025-10-15 11:23:06');
